---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title={`Privacy | ${SITE.name}`} description={`${SITE.name} runs every calculator in your browser. No accounts, no ad trackers, no uploads.`}>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top:32px">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={u('/')}>Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">Privacy</span></nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated 31 October 2026</p>
      <p>{SITE.name} has no accounts, no ad scripts and no cross-site trackers. Calculators run entirely in your browser. The menu engineering tool reads your sales file <strong>on your device</strong>; it is never uploaded.</p>
      <h2>Network requests this site makes</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Request</th><th>When</th><th>Contains your data?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody><tr><td>Pages, scripts and styles</td><td>When you open a page</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Visit statistics (Cloudflare Web Analytics)</td><td>When you open a page</td><td>No personal data or files: page address, referring site, browser and country</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Calculator inputs are stored only in the page address (so you can share a result). Nothing is sent to us. A strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> prevents scripts from sending data to any other server, except the cookie-free visit counter described below.</p>
      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>Some pages recommend products through plain affiliate links. Clicking one takes you to the partner’s website, which applies its own privacy policy. A short tag only tells the partner which page of ours you came from. See our <a href={u('/disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>The site sets no cookies. We count visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which does not use cookies or local storage and does not follow you across websites. It records the page address you opened, the site you came from, your browser type and country, so we can see which tools are useful. It never receives your files. If advertising is ever added, it will use a certified consent banner where the law requires one.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or a security concern? Contact {SITE.author} via the <a href={u('/about/#contact')}>About page</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
